<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Khadas Edge1 - device compatibility matrix.

  The mirror of vintf/manifest.xml: the manifest says what this vendor image
  *provides*, this matrix says what it *requires of the framework*. BoardConfig.mk
  names it as DEVICE_MATRIX_FILE, and check_vintf checks it against the framework
  manifest.

  type="device" - not "framework", which is the FCM that lives in AOSP and states
  what the framework requires of vendors.

  It requires nothing, and that is correct rather than lazy. Nothing on the vendor
  side of this board calls into a framework HAL: every HAL here is an AOSP one
  talking to a mainline kernel driver, so there is no framework-provided interface
  this image depends on.

  It did carry one requirement, <vendor-ndk><version>34</version>, and check_vintf
  rejected it:

    ERROR: files are incompatible: Framework manifest and device compatibility
    matrix are incompatible: Vndk version 34 is not supported. Supported versions
    in framework manifest are: []

  An empty list, not a mismatched number: this release provides no VNDK snapshot at
  all. VNDK is deprecated, and AOSP wires that deprecation up in two steps that are
  easy to miss because neither says anything.

    core/envsetup.mk:53-58   KEEP_VNDK defaults to false when the release config
                             sets RELEASE_DEPRECATE_VNDK, and to true otherwise.
    core/config.mk:1266-1273 when KEEP_VNDK is not true, BOARD_VNDK_VERSION and
                             PLATFORM_VNDK_VERSION are cleared - assigned empty,
                             with no warning.

  So BOARD_VNDK_VERSION := current in BoardConfig.mk was discarded before anything
  read it, the framework manifest listed no versions to match, and this file was
  asking for something that no longer exists. Both are gone. Nothing needs to
  replace them: when a future release keeps VNDK, envsetup.mk:64 sets
  BOARD_VNDK_VERSION := current itself if the board has not.
-->
<compatibility-matrix version="1.0" type="device">
</compatibility-matrix>
